# nova-nix stdenv: the specs the compiler drivers' wrappers give
# gcc-native-x86_64 with -specs, which it reads after its own, skipping a
# line that begins with #.
#
# A spec whose text begins with + and a space is added to the end of the
# spec of that name.  The link spec is in what the driver runs only when it
# links, so every link it makes gets --no-insert-timestamp (ld-wrapper.sh
# says why), and a command that links nothing gets no linker option.  The
# flag is not given on the command line as -Wl,--no-insert-timestamp: a
# -Wl, option is an input file to the driver, so with it gcc -v, which
# prints the configuration and stops, goes on to link a program from no
# object.
*link:
+ --no-insert-timestamp
